From 63ca93f72008e92a025e71633d776a1bc84babbd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 20:45:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban release: match legacy comment events by uid
 write time; stamp rows inside the lock

add_comment took `now` before entering write_txn, so a row waiting on another
writer's lock was stamped seconds before its commented event (5 s and 7 s on
t_0b716b01a47db7f6). The legacy fallback compares those integer stamps within
1 s, so the events stayed "Comment data unavailable" and every --seen release
of the card was refused, while their UUIDv7 uids, minted in the one
transaction, sit 6 ms and 1 ms apart.

- add_comment stamps the row after the lock, like its event (producer fix).
- _resolve's legacy fallback also accepts a same-author row whose UUIDv7 write
  time is within 1 s of the event's: the existing tolerance on the writer's
  own clock. Non-v7 or missing uids keep the old rule only.
- test_delayed_legacy_local_writer now drifts both clocks, so it keeps testing
  run provenance rather than the co-minted case the new rule proves.
- Review nits on the redaction proof: ImportError fails closed; docstring says
  masking is many-to-one; the negative test covers all three entry paths.

Replay tests use the two live shapes on promote, unblock and the agent tool;
they and the producer test fail without the source change.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
